    "description": "Shown in the 'after' pane when generating or rendering the latest preview failed (#58)."
  },
  "previewStaticFrameNote": "This is a time-based effect; the preview shows a single still frame rather than the motion.",
  "@previewStaticFrameNote": {
    "description": "Shown under the preview panes when the selected filter is time-dependent (e.g. vertigo, BPPV rotation) and the static preview can't show its motion (#60)."
  },

  "changePattern": "Change pattern",
  "@changePattern": {
    "description": "Button that regenerates the random pattern of a seed parameter (the seed number itself is never shown, #80)."
  },
  "experimentalBadge": "Experimental",
  "@experimentalBadge": {
    "description": "Badge on filters that are visualizations rather than a validated model of a condition (currently tetrachromacy, #80). The set is defined by VisionFilterEntry.isExperimental."
  },
  "provenanceModelHeading": "Model and source",
  "@provenanceModelHeading": {
    "description": "Heading of the collapsible section showing the model and citation that sensus gives for the selected filter (#80)."
  },
  "provenanceLimitationsHeading": "What this can't show",
  "@provenanceLimitationsHeading": {
    "description": "Heading of the collapsible section showing sensus's description of what the simulation cannot represent (#80)."
  },
  "provenanceNoCitation": "sensus does not list a source for this filter.",
  "@provenanceNoCitation": {
    "description": "Shown in the model-and-source section when sensus's citation() is null. Null means sensus has no documented primary source (it never invents one); it does not claim the filter is wrong (#80)."
  },
  "provenanceSourceNote": "Metadata from the simulation library sensus. Not medically reviewed.",
  "@provenanceSourceNote": {
    "description": "Attribution line under the model/source and limitations text, which are sensus's own wording (#80). Must stay consistent with consultDisclaimer (no medical review)."
  },
  "provenanceEnglishOriginalNote": "Shown as provided by sensus, in English.",
  "@provenanceEnglishOriginalNote": {
    "description": "Shown only when the UI language is not English: sensus supplies the citation and limitations text in English only, and ue does not translate medical wording (#80)."
  },
  "provenanceAboutFilter": "The information below is about the \"{filter}\" filter.",
  "@provenanceAboutFilter": {
    "description": "Shown above the model/source and limitations rows when the heading is an experience preset, so it is clear which underlying filter the information is for (#80).",
    "placeholders": {
      "filter": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "changePatternFor": "Change pattern ({param})",
  "@changePatternFor": {
    "description": "Screen-reader label of the seed button (read instead of the on-screen text); names the parameter so that several buttons can be told apart (#80).",
    "placeholders": {
      "param": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "exportExperimentalNotice": "Experimental visualization",
  "@exportExperimentalNotice": {
    "description": "Second notice line burned into the exported PNG of an experimental filter (currently tetrachromacy), next to the simulation notice (#80). The set is VisionFilterEntry.isExperimental."
  },
  "exportSimulationNotice": "Simulation (approximation)",
  "@exportSimulationNotice": {
    "description": "One line burned into every exported PNG caption so that the image is never mistaken for a real photo or a measurement (#80)."
  },

  "prevalenceLabel": "Prevalence: {value}",
  "@prevalenceLabel": {
    "description": "Prevalence line shown for the selected color-vision type.",
    "placeholders": {
      "value": { "type": "String" }
    }
  },
  "strengthLabel": "Strength: {percent}%",
  "@strengthLabel": {
    "description": "Strength of the selected advanced filter as a percentage.",
    "placeholders": {
      "percent": { "type": "int" }
    }
  },
  "resetToRecommendedStrength": "Reset to recommended",
  "@resetToRecommendedStrength": {
    "description": "Button that resets the selected filter's strength and parameters back to sensus's recommended_strength and the catalog's default parameter values (#77)."
  },
  "strengthCautionMarkerNote": "Past the mark at {percent}%, the image shows the most advanced stage. At 100% strength almost the whole visual field is lost and only a small central area stays visible.",
  "@strengthCautionMarkerNote": {
    "description": "Always-visible caption under the strength slider of a filter with an upper-limit caution (currently tunnel_vision, #51 note 1 / #66). Explains the tick mark drawn at the caution threshold.",
    "placeholders": {
      "percent": { "type": "int" }
    }
  },
  "strengthCautionNearLimit": "Approaching the upper limit. The image goes almost black because this reproduces the most advanced stage, where nearly all of the visual field is lost. It is not a malfunction.",
  "@strengthCautionNearLimit": {
    "description": "Warning that replaces the caption when strength is at or above the caution threshold (#66). Must make clear the near-black image is by design."
  },
  "consultEarly": "If these symptoms continue, consider talking to a healthcare professional.",
  "@consultEarly": {
    "description": "Gentle prompt for early-consultation-urgency conditions. Deliberately names no medical department (many of these filters, e.g. vertigo, aren't an eye complaint) (#76). Must not alarm or over-promise."
  },
  "consultEmergency": "If these symptoms appear suddenly, seek medical care right away.",
  "@consultEmergency": {
    "description": "Firmer prompt for emergency-urgency conditions. Deliberately names no medical department (#76). Must be accurate and not alarmist."
  },
  "consultDisclaimer": "This is general guidance, not a medical diagnosis. It has not been reviewed by a medical professional. Source: sensus (a simulation library)'s public documentation, Medical notes.",
  "@consultDisclaimer": {
    "description": "Full disclaimer shown in the UI (right-hand adjustment column, always shown with the consult note for both advanced filters and experience presets) alongside every consult note, stating this app does not diagnose and has not had medical review, with a citation to sensus's own Medical notes doc (#76; names sensus as a simulation library and its docs as the source). The actual URL is shown separately as selectable text (ConsultNoticeBlock / ConsultDisclaimerFooter), not embedded in this string."
  },
  "consultDisclaimerShort": "Not a diagnosis; not medically reviewed. Source: sensus Medical notes",
  "@consultDisclaimerShort": {
    "description": "Compact disclaimer burned into the exported PNG caption (#76). Must fit both the non-diagnosis disclaimer AND the citation in one short line — kept short so the caption band stays small. The UI uses the longer consultDisclaimer instead."
  },
  "escalationHeaderEarly": "Consider seeing a doctor if:",
  "@escalationHeaderEarly": {
    "description": "Header introducing the EarlyConsultation-tier escalation conditions (Filter::urgency_escalation() / HearingFilter::urgency_escalation(), #76)."
  },
  "escalationHeaderEmergency": "See a doctor right away if:",
  "@escalationHeaderEmergency": {
    "description": "Header introducing the Emergency-tier escalation conditions (#76). Vision filters never escalate to Emergency today, but HearingFilter's hearing-loss family does — this header is ready for that UI (#80)."
  },
